Found by M3's delta review of PR #1287 (comment 2026-11-12T23:03Z). It was posted after #1287 merged at 23:00Z, so this is on main now.

**What happens.** `install_panic_hook` in `crates/ui/src/win_console.rs` (about lines 135-144) fires at panic time, before any `catch_unwind` runs. The app catches panics on purpose in several places:
- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/gpu_init.rs:166` (the GPU probe);
- `shell.rs:910` and `shell_window.rs:220`;
- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step.rs:133` (a STEP kernel panic turns into a clean import error);
- `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs:155`;
- `crates/kernel/src/truck_impl.rs`.

So when the app is started by double-click on Windows, a *handled* panic still pops a modal "CamCraft stopped unexpectedly" box. A bad STEP import is one example. The box blocks that thread and uses up the once-per-process flag, so a later real failure shows nothing.

A second, smaller case: if `AttachConsole` succeeds but the `CONOUT$` open fails (around lines 95-97), `CONSOLE_ATTACHED` stays true. Output then goes nowhere, and no box is shown.

**Done means:**
- the global hook is gone, and on Windows `main` wraps `camcraft_ui::run` in `catch_unwind`, showing the box only for a panic that escapes `run` or a non-zero exit with no console;
- a failed `CONOUT$` open counts as "no console";
- any pure part (payload to text) has a unit test;
- the PR's Windows hand-check list includes "a bad STEP import by double-click shows no box".

Add one page listing every keyboard shortcut and mouse action in CamCraft, with a column each for Windows/Linux and macOS.

Cover:
- File, Edit and Run shortcuts (new, open model, open project, save, save as, post, undo, redo, copy and paste an operation, delete, frame/fit);
- the viewport mouse (orbit, pan, zoom, and the trackpad equivalents on a Mac);
- picking modifiers (add an edge, pick a whole loop, box-select, deselect);
- right-click and context menus (Control-click or two-finger click on a Mac).

Take the bindings from the code (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs`, `edge_pick.rs`, `interact.rs`, the ribbon tips), not from memory. Where the app uses egui's `command` modifier, the macOS column is Cmd. Where it reads the real Ctrl, check on a Mac whether Control-click arrives as a right-click, and say so.

Related: #1236 (Mac equivalents throughout the site) finds the Windows-only wording on other pages; this page is the one table those pages can link to.

Done means: a shortcuts and mouse page in the guide, every entry checked against the code, with Mac and Windows/Linux columns, linked from first-run.md.

Found while working #869 (Air coolant mode). An operation's coolant (`Off` / `Flood` / `Mist` / `Air` / `Through tool`) is set in the GUI through the undoable `EditOperationParams::with_coolant` (`CommandKind::EditOperationCoolant`), but no MCP tool or script verb reaches it. A headless agent cannot ask for air on a Carvera, or for Off on a dry cut.

**Done means:**
- an MCP tool (e.g. `set_operation_coolant { name, coolant: "off" | "flood" | "mist" | "air" | "through-tool" }`) that runs the same undoable command, so undo/redo hold headlessly;
- an unknown word is refused by name;
- the camcraft-mcp skill's tool table lists it;
- pinned by a test that sets Air through MCP and undoes it.
